    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T03:05:54Z",
    "body": "Coordinator decision for the 0.25.0 site (recorded unattended; the file `docs/decisions/3271-site-redeploy.md` follows in the workflow PR):\n\n- The tag v0.25.0 does not move, and there is no patch cut.\n- `release.yml` can deploy the site only from a tag run in which `site` and `publish` both succeed. A re-run of the v0.25.0 run uses the tagged tree, so its site tests fail again.\n- Chosen: one workflow PR on `main` adds the input `site_only` to the existing `workflow_dispatch`. With that input, only `site` and `pages` run, from the dispatched ref. `publish` stays tag-only and does not change. The dispatch runs once on a new branch `site/v0.25.0`: v0.25.0 plus only the docs and test fixes of PR #3274 that apply to the 0.25.0 tree.\n- Dropped: a site build from `main`. It would show \"CamCraft 0.25.0\" but describe features that came after the tag (V-Carve, the deburr multi-pass, the router materials).\n- Fallback: if the owner does not add the branch policy below, the 0.25.0 site content ships with the deploy of v0.26.0.\n\nOwner ask (a repository settings change, not a merge): add deployment branch policy `site/*` to environment github-pages (Settings > Environments > github-pages, or `gh api -X POST repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/environments/github-pages/deployment-branch-policies -f name='site/*' -f type=branch`)\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
